  "description": "Unison outer and list transitions, retained help, page jumps, assignment and removal, closing and reopening, plus every settled variants check.",
  "registration": "Reuses the unchanged silent unison-variants-paired-v2/dolphin recording and its native/Dolphin fixture pins and source input replay. Native update 64 registers source VI zero using the complete equipment-transitions-keyboard ambient origin. Read-only reinspection of the Unison savestate matches the equipment source exactly for controlled actor, all ambient actors, particles, RNG, clocks, field animations, skit, eyes and background script registries. Native loads story 2500 to initialize the shared school field, then changes the checkpoint and event story to 1403000 at update 76 after Main opens; source already has story 1403000. The origin-0 native capture is registration only and is not paired while these story values differ. Source Y requests Main at VI 11 and first presents it at VI 12, mapped to native update 76; subsequent action edges use source poll/2 + 1, mapped to VI + 64, with native release on the next update. All 4,150 observed VIs are contiguous and satisfy UI clock = 38084 + VI and effect clock = 37551 + VI, with no skipped source clocks, removed waits or presentation/effect advances. Exact timestamp inspection found 4,040 unique native-resolution lossless FFV1 presentations spanning VIs 0-4148; all timestamps satisfy NTSC VI quantization. Requested VIs 184, 187, 190, 193, 195, 198, 1211, 1214, 1217, 1220, 1223 have no video presentation and are omitted without shifting inputs or substituting neighboring images. All 24 old settled frames remain. Unison is active at VIs 183-3382 and from 3463 onward; unison_state checks every selected active frame, including retained outgoing description, against watched mode/slot, row/first, postdraw scroll, character/count, all nine members' shortcuts, selected member choices and retained description. Every required word was audited in the per-VI observations and watcher map before enabling the gate. effect_clock_state checks every paired frame. The older recording has no Main/page/list/help fade or RNG word observations, so numerical transition-phase, Main and random-state gates are deliberately absent; full-frame images still cover their visible output with the unchanged 8/1% tolerance. It contains page jumps and list/help transitions but no nonzero animated row-scroll phase, so signed row-boundary scrolling is not covered. No new Dolphin, GPU or audio run was performed to author this case.",
